column17:
1. To identify the optimal ICT-related feature set and their relative importance for reading in the blended learning setting; 
2. to investigate the relationships between student-level ICT-related factors and students’ reading performance;
3. to examine the association between school-level ICT-related factors and students’ reading performance; and 
4. to probe into the moderation effect of school-level ICT-related factors on the relationship between student-level factors and reading performance.

column20:
1. An overview and classification of the research landscape; 
2. A review of data sources (LMS, MOOCs, OER, Social Media); 
3. An analysis of data collection, datasets, and mining techniques; 
4. A technical review of Big Data architectures (Hadoop, Spark, Samza); 
5. A deep dive into analytics types (predictive, collaborative, visual, and immersive). Second, to validate technological challenges, the authors conducted an empirical case study using graph based analytics to detect unobserved prerequisite dependencies between courses, training models on data from one university and testing them on others.

column26:
1. Presents an overview and classification of Big education research to show the full landscape in this field, which also gives a concise summary of the overall scope of this paper; 
2. Presents a discussion for the various data sources from education platforms or systems including learning management systems (LMS), massive open online courses (MOOC), learning object repository (LOR), Open Course Ware (OCW), open educational resources (OER), social media, linked data and mobile learning contributing to Big education data; 
3. Presents the data collection, data mining and databases in Big education data;

